.TH MU2EDAQ_COMMANDLINE_TOOLS 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq_commandline_tools \- Python API for the Mu2e DAQ command line tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B from mu2edaq_commandline_tools import config, cli, __version__
.PP
.BI "config.load(" "explicit_path=None, overrides=None, environ=None" ") -> dict"
.BI "config.find_config(" "explicit=None" ") -> pathlib.Path | None"
.BI "config.config_search_paths(" "explicit=None" ") -> Iterable[Path]"
.BI "config.load_file(" path ") -> dict"
.BI "config.load_env(" "environ=None" ") -> dict"
.BI "config.DEFAULTS" "  # dict of built-in defaults"
.PP
.BI "cli.main(" "argv=None" ") -> int"
.BI "cli.COMMANDS" "  # dict of name -> Command(help, add_arguments, run)"
.PP
.B from mu2edaq_commandline_tools.otsdaq import OtsdaqClient, resolve_instance
.PP
.BI "resolve_instance(" "cfg, **overrides" ") -> InstanceConfig"
.BI "OtsdaqClient(" "instance" ")"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SS Configuration
.B config.load()
builds the effective configuration by applying, in increasing order of
precedence: the built-in
.BR DEFAULTS ,
the YAML config file, the
.BR MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_ *
environment, and
.IR overrides .
.PP
.I overrides
carries the parsed command line. Entries whose value is
.B None
are ignored, so an argparse option the user did not give does not clobber a
lower-precedence source. Keys not present in
.B DEFAULTS
are ignored from every source.
.PP
The returned dict holds one extra key,
.BR _config_file ,
naming the file that was read, or
.B None
when none was found. Keys beginning with an underscore are metadata, not
settings.
.PP
.B load()
raises
.B ValueError
when the YAML file's top level, its
.B otsdaq
block, or an
.B otsdaq.instances
entry is not a mapping,
.B OSError
when it cannot be read, and
.B RuntimeError
when PyYAML is missing.
A YAML syntax error propagates as
.BR yaml.YAMLError ,
which
.B cli.main()
does not catch.
A config file that does not exist is not an error, including an
.I explicit_path
that does not exist: the defaults are then used without searching further.
.PP
Environment values for
.B discovery_timeout
and
.B color
are coerced to float and bool; a value that fails coercion is kept as the raw
string.
An empty environment variable counts as unset.
There is no
.I .env
file layer.
.PP
.I environ
defaults to
.BR os.environ ;
pass a dict to make tests hermetic.
.SS Adding a tool
Register a subcommand in
.BR cli.COMMANDS .
A
.B Command
is a named tuple of a help string, an optional hook that adds argparse
options to the subparser, and a run hook called as
.RI run( args ", " cfg )
that returns a process exit status:
.PP
.nf
.RS
from mu2edaq_commandline_tools.cli import COMMANDS, Command

def _add_ping(parser):
    parser.add_argument("host")

def cmd_ping(args, cfg):
    print("pinging %s on %s" % (args.host, cfg["cluster"]))
    return 0

COMMANDS["ping"] = Command("check a node responds", _add_ping, cmd_ping)
.RE
.fi
.PP
The tool then appears in
.BR "mu2edaq-tools list" ,
gets the global options and config resolution for free, and needs no changes
to the dispatcher.
.SS otsdaq
.B resolve_instance()
selects a named
.B otsdaq.instances
profile and merges, lowest first: top-level
.B otsdaq
keys, the profile, the
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_OTSDAQ_*
environment, and the keyword arguments.
It validates the origins, derives Slow Controls (gateway port + 1) and TFM
(gateway host, port 3047) when they are not given, and reads the CookieCode
from
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_OTSDAQ_COOKIE
or the owner-only
.IR cookie_file .
A CA bundle from any layer forces
.B verify_tls
on.
The returned frozen dataclass
.B InstanceConfig
carries the CookieCode in its
.B cookie_code
field, which its default
.B repr()
includes.
.PP
.B OtsdaqClient
provides synchronous typed reads for current state, run info, DAQ report/state,
runtime macro inventory, PV data/settings, alarms, and console/system messages.
Every request is an HTTP POST.
Its
.B request()
method retains both exact XML and a normalized representation and is not
restricted to read-only RequestTypes; it adds the CookieCode as a form field
only when the LID is 281.
Errors are raised as subclasses of
.BR OtsdaqError :
.BR OtsdaqConfigError ,
.BR OtsdaqTransportError ,
.BR OtsdaqHTTPError ,
.BR OtsdaqProtocolError .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.RS
from mu2edaq_commandline_tools import config

cfg = config.load(overrides={"cluster": args.cluster})
print(cfg["cluster"], "from", cfg["_config_file"] or "defaults")
.RE
.fi
